    choose: [['Put the statement back (in / towards) context.', 'in'], ['Riku puts a proposal forward for (review / reviewed).', 'review'], ['The clip omits a qualifying (argument / argued).', 'argument'], ['Keep public remarks separate (from / into) private disclosures.', 'from'], ['Ms. Fujimoto agreed (to take / taking) the suggestion to her company.', 'to take'], ['An edited clip does not (identify / identifies) its uploader.', 'identify']],
    choices: [['What was Daisuke’s fuller public position?', 'Business risks should be met with support and fair opportunities to adapt.', 'Struggling businesses should be abandoned.', 'A'], ['What is the advisory group’s status?', 'It is already established with binding powers.', 'A suggestion the representative will bring to the company.', 'B'], ['What does Leila’s authorised recording establish?', 'She recorded the public discussion with permission and clear notices.', 'She must have created and uploaded the misleading edit.', 'A'], ['What remains open at the end?', 'That the clip is being shared.', 'Who uploaded it and how the team will respond.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: 'You are Emi. Your tutor is Leila. A clipped forum statement omits Daisuke’s support argument. The advisory-group idea awaits company consideration, and the uploader is unknown. Daisuke’s private debt disclosure remains outside public use.', task: 'Reconstruct the public argument, state the actual meeting outcome and propose what needs checking before a response.', roles: ['Leila', 'Emi'], lines: ['Emi, what did Daisuke say after acknowledging that some businesses might not survive?', 'Why does the missing argument matter to the caption’s claim?', 'What did Ms. Fujimoto actually agree to do about the advisory group?', 'Can my recording identify who uploaded the short version?', 'Do public remarks authorise use of an earlier private conversation?', 'What should we verify before describing a public response as completed?'], evidence: 'A week later public forum. Leila records with organisers’ permission and clear notices, not a blanket release of private sources. Daisuke public remarks recognise business risk whether redevelopment or not, then insist on support/fair negotiation/adaptation. No private debt details shared. Riku proposes advisory group to review relocation proposals/communicate concerns; Ms. Fujimoto only agrees to bring suggestion back. No final agreement or formed group. Unknown uploader, clipped quote and misleading caption, online one hour with sharing but no exact counts, motive, manipulation proof or completed correction. End unresolved without importing Level 7 villains or assuming Leila is editor.', useful: ['The public argument was ..., not simply ...', 'The clip leaves out ...', 'The agreed next step is only ...', 'That does not identify ...', 'Before responding, we should ...'] },
    topics: [['CONTEXT', ['How can an authentic quotation support a misleading impression?', 'What surrounding argument should a fair summary preserve?', 'Why avoid adding private facts to correct a public excerpt?']], ['COMMUNITY PROPOSALS', ['What is the difference between considering a group and establishing it?', 'How can a meeting make progress without final agreement?', 'What should be checked before announcing a commitment?']], ['RESPONSIBLE RESPONSES', ['Why compare a clip with the public recording?', 'What does sharing activity leave unknown?', 'How can a team respond carefully without guessing the uploader’s identity?']]],
    trivia: '“Bring a suggestion to the company” describes a next step in consideration. It does not mean the company has accepted it. That difference matters when reporting the forum’s progress alongside its unresolved questions.', triviaQuestion: ['Does agreeing to take the suggestion back establish the advisory group?', 'No. It confirms a step towards review, not formation.'],
    closing: 'The forum identifies proposals but reaches no final agreement. Daisuke’s public call for support is reduced to a misleading clip, while his private debt remains excluded. Leila alerts Emi as sharing begins. The uploader, response and redevelopment decisions remain unresolved.',
